@* A quiet invitation to the Twenty Four game, sliding in from the right edge.

   It exists because the nav link says "Twenty Four" and nothing else — a visitor has
   no way to know that is a game, let alone one they can play all afternoon. The daily
   challenge is over in a minute; this is the only route to more.

   Deliberately not a modal: it must never block the puzzle. No backdrop, no focus
   steal, no Escape trap. Someone mid-thought on a hard teaser should be able to ignore
   it completely and lose nothing. *@

<aside class="tfn @(Visible ? "tfn-in" : "")" aria-label="More puzzles">
    <button class="tfn-close" @onclick="OnDismiss" aria-label="Dismiss">✕</button>

    <p class="tfn-kicker">Want another?</p>
    <h3 class="tfn-title">Twenty&nbsp;Four</h3>
    <p class="tfn-body">
        Four numbers, one target: make <strong>24</strong> using each of them exactly
        once. A fresh hand every time — play as many as you like.
    </p>
    <a class="tfn-go" href="twentyfour">Give it a go →</a>
</aside>

@code {
    /// <summary>Slides in when true. Kept as a class toggle so the exit animates too.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Visible { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public EventCallback OnDismiss { get; set; }
}
